invalid type: string "SECTION 14: Examples of returns\n\nThese examples are for a deposit of one lakh rupees, with interest added every three months. They are approximate.\nAt four percent for twenty years, one lakh rupees becomes about 2 lakh 21 thousand rupees.\nAt four percent for twenty-five years, one lakh rupees becomes about 2 lakh 70 thousand rupees.\ned by the bank executive.", expected f